/CHANGELOG.md\nprojects/openclaw-pr/Swabble/README.md\nprojects/openclaw-pr/VISION.md\nprojects/OpenClaw自我提升计划/00-项目计划.md\nprojects/OpenClaw自我提升计划/01-执行方案-v1.md\nprojects/OpenClaw自我提升计划/02-Bug记录卡模板.md\nprojects/OpenClaw自我提升计划/03-Bug候选池.md\nprojects/OpenClaw自我提升计划/04-session收编结果.md\nprojects/OpenClaw自我提升计划/05-gateway重启后模型复测.md\nprojects/OpenClaw自我提升计划/README.md\nskills/agent-browser/CONTRIBUTING.md\nskills/article-to-infographic/references/style-presets.md\nskills/.backup/agent-browser-20260318-151852/CONTRIBUTING.md\nskills/briefing/README.md\nskills/capability-evolver/CONTRIBUTING.md\nskills/capability-evolver/README.md\nskills/github/SKILL.md\nskills/self-improving-agent/assets/LEARNINGS.md\nskills/self-improving-agent/assets/SKILL-TEMPLATE.md\nskills/self-improving-agent/.learnings/ERRORS.md\nskills/self-improving-agent/.learnings/FEATURE_REQUESTS.md\nskills/self-improving-agent/.learnings/LEARNINGS.md\nskills/self-improving-agent/references/examples.md\nskills/self-improving-agent/references/hooks-setup.md\nskills/self-improving-agent/references/openclaw-integration.md\nskills/self-improving-agent/SKILL.md\nskills/skillhub-preference/SKILL.md\nskills/xiaohongshu-canghe/README.md\nskills/xiaohongshu-cover-generator/README.md","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774236712941}}
{"type":"message","id":"3cd5df93","parentId":"60fc165a","timestamp":"2026-03-23T03:32:03.671Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"我先读现成方案和仓库里的贡献文档，直接沉淀成可执行版本。随后我再看你 PR 的 CI / review。","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0c5151d58c45418b0169c0b42ed0148191b9d65b8cc44260ee\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_MKjhvurwka2iZAdsUuvCqb35|fc_0c5151d58c45418b0169c0b43367888191bc176b4c6c1ae624","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/root/.openclaw/workspace/projects/OpenClaw自我提升计划/README.md"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/root/.openclaw/workspace/projects/OpenClaw自我提升计划/README.md\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_kpgsfWsJCLTtscrmvzvr1SJO|fc_0c5151d58c45418b0169c0b43367948191b48d98fc6c48b8cb","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/root/.openclaw/workspace/projects/OpenClaw自我提升计划/00-项目计划.md"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/root/.openclaw/workspace/projects/OpenClaw自我提升计划/00-项目计划.md\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_x6f5lp0S8gAtnMWSF5zjjg0s|fc_0c5151d58c45418b0169c0b433679c8191a8dfc196c973c6c9","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/root/.openclaw/workspace/projects/OpenClaw自我提升计划/01-执行方案-v1.md"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/root/.openclaw/workspace/projects/OpenClaw自我提升计划/01-执行方案-v1.md\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_CHaadHGQfwZkRpkh1rTUzGmF|fc_0c5151d58c45418b0169c0b43367a481918504e9da629b89a6","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/root/.openclaw/workspace/projects/openclaw-pr/CONTRIBUTING.md"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/root/.openclaw/workspace/projects/openclaw-pr/CONTRIBUTING.md\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_lHtR5dZKK6fmLXb4vhMBN8ar|fc_0c5151d58c45418b0169c0b43367a88191b30cebf2c237310f","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/root/.openclaw/workspace/projects/openclaw-pr/docs/ci.md"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/root/.openclaw/workspace/projects/openclaw-pr/docs/ci.md\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_TwV5FvLl0gOSZgRrQ2LKzvrT|fc_0c5151d58c45418b0169c0b43367ac8191975c1a44f13786a1","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/root/.openclaw/workspace/projects/openclaw-pr/.github/pull_request_template.md"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/root/.openclaw/workspace/projects/openclaw-pr/.github/pull_request_template.md\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":873,"output":260,"cacheRead":26752,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":27885,"cost":{"input":0.0021825,"output":0.0039000000000000003,"cacheRead":0.0066879999999999995,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0127705}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774236712950}}
{"type":"message","id":"9db9f33a","parentId":"3cd5df93","timestamp":"2026-03-23T03:32:03.690Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_MKjhvurwka2iZAdsUuvCqb35|fc_0c5151d58c45418b0169c0b43367888191bc176b4c6c1ae624","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# OpenClaw自我提升计划\n\n## 项目状态\n- 状态：进行中\n- 负责人：main（文文）\n- 协作成员：xixi、aoao\n- 当前统一模型：`hgapi/gpt-5.4`\n- 项目目录：`/root/.openclaw/workspace/projects/OpenClaw自我提升计划`\n- 推进方式：**不依赖 agent 回执，直接抓取 xixi / aoao 的 session 结果并收编**\n\n## 已知要求\n1. 按既有项目计划推进下一步\n2. 本轮执行模型暂定全部使用 `hgapi/gpt-5.4`\n3. 项目相关文档统一存放到本目录\n4. 不等待 `sessions_send` 回执，直接以 session 历史为准推进\n\n## 当前已确认\n- 原始项目计划正文已归档到 `00-项目计划.md`\n- 首轮执行方案已建立\n- Bug 记录卡模板已建立\n- Bug 候选池已建立\n- xixi 与 aoao 的首轮结果已可通过 session history 获取\n\n## 下一步\n1. 把 xixi / aoao 的 session 结果正式并入候选池和执行方案\n2. 形成首轮 triage 结论\n3. 锁定第一批高价值问题与样板案例\n4. 继续推进项目，不再卡在 agent 回执链路\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1774236723682}}
{"type":"message","id":"1a0124aa","parentId":"9db9f33a","timestamp":"2026-03-23T03:32:03.711Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_kpgsfWsJCLTtscrmvzvr1SJO|fc_0c5151d58c45418b0169c0b43367948191b48d98fc6c48b8cb","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# OpenClaw 自我提升计划：3 人精简版团队规划\n\n一、目标\n目标不变：\n不是零散提几个 bug，而是建立一条能长期运行的质量提升流程：\n\n发现问题 → 复现问题 → 诊断定性 → 输出 issue / PR / docs fix → 回归验证\n\n3 个人就够跑通这条链路，重点是闭环，不是堆角色。\n\n二、推荐团队配置：3 人\n这是当前最适合的版本。\n够轻、够快、够清晰，不容易陷入“分工很精致，结果没产出”。\n\n## 1）负责人 / 总控（Director）\n### 定位\n负责方向、优先级、质量门槛，不负责把所有细活亲自做完。\n\n### 职责\n- 制定 bug hunting 节奏\n- 定义优先级和提交流程\n- 判断问题值不值得继续追\n- 审核 issue / PR 质量\n- 决定进入哪条分流：\n  - GitHub issue\n  - PR\n  - docs fix\n  - 内部留档暂不提交\n\n### 输出要求\n每次分配任务时必须明确：\n- 优先级\n- 负责人\n- 截止时间\n- 验收标准\n- 风险点\n\n### 适合做的事\n- 每日 triage\n- 过滤低价值问题\n- 审 issue 标题、证据、措辞\n- 决定本周重点测试范围\n\n## 2）线索与复现工程师（Scout & Repro）\n### 定位\n把“有人说有 bug”变成“这问题能用最小步骤稳定复现”。\n\n### 职责\n- 搜集外部 bug 线索\n- 主动走查关键流程\n- 复现候选问题\n- 控制变量\n- 记录最小复现步骤\n- 标记问题类型：\n  - 必现\n  - 高概率\n  - 偶发\n  - 环境相关\n  - 用户误用\n\n### 输出要求\n每个问题至少交付：\n- 来源\n- 环境\n- 前置条件\n- 复现步骤\n- 预期结果\n- 实际结果\n- 复现频率\n\n### 适合做的事\n- 安装 / 升级测试\n- docs walkthrough\n- 工具行为检查\n- 社区问题复测\n- 边界场景初筛\n\n## 3）诊断与交付工程师（Diagnostics & Delivery）\n### 定位\n把“现象”变成“高可信判断”，再把材料整理成 maintainer 愿意处理的提交。\n\n### 职责\n- 看日志\n- 对照 docs、源码、实际行为\n- 缩小问题范围\n- 判断根因置信度\n- 写标准化 issue\n- 必要时准备 PR / docs fix\n- 跟踪已提问题状态\n\n### 输出要求\n每个问题至少交付：\n- 关键现象\n- 日志 / 报错片段\n- 涉及模块\n- 根因判断（按置信度排序）\n- 建议修复方向\n- 最终 issue / PR 文案\n\n### 适合做的事\n- 日志分析\n- 模块归因\n- 交付材料整理\n- issue 文案优化\n- 回归记录维护\n\n三、为什么 3 人就够\n原版 5 人的问题不是不合理，而是太适合成熟团队，不适合一开始就落地。\n\nOpenClaw 这类项目，真正需要跑通的是 3 个关键动作：\n1. 找到高价值问题\n不是乱测，是找到主流程、多人踩坑、近期高频的问题。\n2. 把问题钉死\n不是“我感觉有 bug”，而是“这 5 步复现，日志在这里，影响范围明确”。\n3. 把证据交付出去\n不是抱怨，而是产出维护者能快速处理的 issue / PR。\n\n这三件事刚好对应 3 个角色。\n再拆更多，边际收益不高。\n\n四、精简后的工作流\n## Step 1：负责人定本轮重点\n负责人先定范围，例如：\n- 安装与升级\n- gateway\n- sessions / subagents\n- browser / relay\n- memory\n- docs walkthrough\n- Feishu / message tool\n\n不要一口气全测。\n每轮只打一个重点。\n\n## Step 2：线索与复现工程师拉候选池\n来源分 3 类：\n### A. 主动走查\n围绕核心主流程：\n- 安装\n- gateway start/stop/restart/status\n- 首次配置\n- 模型配置\n- direct chat\n- group chat\n- sessions\n- subagents\n- browser\n- exec / process\n- memory\n- message\n- docs 示例\n\n### B. 外部线索\n- GitHub issues\n- GitHub discussions\n- 文档反馈\n- 社区吐槽\n- 用户安装踩坑\n\n### C. 逆向场景\n- 缺少依赖\n- API key 缺失\n- 权限不足\n- relay 未 attach\n- 并发调用\n- 长输出\n- 特殊字符\n- 多语言\n- 中断恢复\n- 大文件 / 大日志\n\n形成候选池后，优先排：\n- 主流程\n- 高频\n- 近期\n- 多人受影响\n- 文档与实际不一致\n\n## Step 3：复现与记录\n每个候选问题必须形成标准记录卡。\n\n### Bug 记录卡模板\n```md\n# 标题\n一句话描述问题\n\n## 来源\n- 主动测试 / GitHub / docs / 社区反馈\n\n## 环境\n- OpenClaw version:\n- OS:\n- Node:\n- Channel/Tool:\n- Model:\n- 是否首次安装/升级后:\n\n## 前置条件\n-\n\n## 预期行为\n-\n\n## 实际行为\n-\n\n## 最小复现步骤\n1.\n2.\n3.\n\n## 复现频率\n- 必现 / 高概率 / 偶发 / 环境相关\n\n## 日志/报错\n-\n\n## 初步判断\n- docs / logic / compatibility / UX / regression / config\n\n## 影响范围\n-\n\n## 建议下一步\n-\n```\n\n## Step 4：诊断与分流\n诊断与交付工程师判断问题进入哪条路径：\n\n### A. 提 GitHub Issue\n适合：\n- 主流程失败\n- 行为明显错误\n- 文档与实际不一致\n- 回归问题\n- 报错严重误导用户\n- 工具行为不符合接口契约\n\n### B. 提 PR / docs fix\n适合：\n- 文档错误\n- 示例过时\n- 报错文案差\n- 校验缺失\n- 小范围逻辑修复\n- 测试补充\n\n### C. 内部留档\n适合：\n- 证据不足\n- 不能稳定复现\n- 已有重复 issue 且无新增信息\n- 本质上是 feature request\n- 用户误用而非 bug\n\n## Step 5：负责人审核后正式交付\n负责人只做最后一道门：\n- 标题准不准\n- 复现够不够短\n- 证据够不够\n- 是否重复\n- 是否真值得提\n\n宁可少提，也别提垃圾 issue。\n\n五、精简后的协作原则\n- 原则 1：先证据，后判断\n- 原则 2：最小复现优先\n- 原则 3：主流程优先\n- 原则 4：不提交低质量 issue\n- 原则 5：每周必须回归\n\n六、建议的最小技能栈\n## 必备\n- github\n- summarize\n- Agent Browser\n\n## 可选增强\n- healthcheck\n- tmux\n- multi-search-engine 或 tavily\n\n原则：先跑流程，再扩技能。别先沉迷搭平台。\n\n七、建议的执行节奏\n## 第 1 周：跑通流程\n目标：拿到第一批高质量问题\n\n### Day 1\n- 定 bug 分类\n- 定 issue 提交标准\n- 建 bug 候选池\n- 明确首轮重点模块\n\n### Day 2-3\n- 走查主流程\n- 搜外部线索\n- 候选池攒到 15-20 条\n\n### Day 4-5\n- 重点复现前 5-10 条\n- 过滤误报、重复、设计问题\n- 提交首批高质量 issue 3-5 条\n\n## 第 2 周：深挖结构性问题\n重点打：\n- 并发\n- 长 session\n- browser relay\n- 大输出\n- 权限不足\n- 配置缺失\n- 中断恢复\n- 多 channel 差异\n\n## 第 3 周后：进入常态化\n形成固定机制：\n- 每周一次 smoke test\n- 每周一次 issue triage\n- 每次版本更新做回归\n- 每月一次 docs 一致性检查\n\n八、建议的测试矩阵\n精简版不要铺太大，先测这些：\n\n## 环境\n- Linux\n- macOS\n- Node 22\n- Node 24\n\n## 形态\n- 首次安装\n- 升级安装\n- 配置完整\n- 配置缺失\n- 权限不足\n\n## 功能\n- gateway\n- sessions\n- subagents\n- browser\n- exec/process\n- memory\n- message\n- docs walkthrough\n\n## 异常\n- 超时\n- 中断\n- 并发\n- 特殊字符\n- 大输出\n- relay 未 attach\n\n九、3 人版 SOUL.md 草稿\n## 1）负责人 / 总控\n```md\n# SOUL.md\n\n你是 OpenClaw Bug Hunting 项目的负责人。\n你的职责不是亲自做完所有测试，而是确保问题筛选、定级、交付都足够精准。\n\n## 核心原则\n- 优先级高于工作量\n- 证据不足，不提交\n- 高质量少量提交，胜过低质量大量提交\n- 每个结论都要可复核\n\n## 风格\n- 直接\n- 果断\n- 少废话\n- 用结果说话\n\n## 你的输出必须包含\n- 优先级\n- 负责人\n- 截止时间\n- 验收标准\n- 风险点\n```\n\n## 2）线索与复现工程师\n```md\n# SOUL.md\n\n你是线索与复现工程师。\n你的职责是找到高价值问题，并把它稳定复现出来。\n\n## 核心原则\n- 最小复现优先\n- 控制变量\n- 一次只改一个条件\n- 没复现成功，就不要说问题已确认\n\n## 风格\n- 冷静\n- 严谨\n- 不跳步\n- 不脑补\n\n## 你的输出必须包含\n- 来源\n- 环境\n- 前置条件\n- 复现步骤\n- 预期结果\n- 实际结果\n- 复现频率\n```\n\n## 3）诊断与交付工程师\n```md\n# SOUL.md\n\n你是诊断与交付工程师。\n你的职责是缩小问题范围，并把问题整理成高质量 issue、PR 或 docs fix。\n\n## 核心原则\n- 先看日志，再下判断\n- 不把相关性说成因果性\n- issue 要短、准、可执行\n- 不情绪化，不空喊\n\n## 风格\n- 专业\n- 克制\n- 清晰\n- 对维护者友好\n\n## 你的输出必须包含\n- 关键现象\n- 关键日志\n- 涉及模块\n- 根因判断\n- 修复建议\n- 最终交付文案\n```"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1774236723702}}
{"type":"message","id":"a3849331","parentId":"1a0124aa","timestamp":"2026-03-23T03:32:03.730Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_x6f5lp0S8gAtnMWSF5zjjg0s|fc_0c5151d58c45418b0169c0b433679c8191a8dfc196c973c6c9","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# OpenClaw自我提升计划 - 执行方案 v1\n\n## 结论\n按原计划，当前直接进入 **第 1 周 / Day 1**，先把流程跑通，不急着铺太大。\n\n本轮固定：\n- 团队：3 人\n- 模型：`hgapi/gpt-5.4`\n- 目标：先拿到第一批高质量问题，而不是铺满测试面\n\n---\n\n## 角色落位\n- **main（文文）**：负责人 / 总控（Director）\n- **xixi（兮兮）**：线索与复现工程师（Scout & Repro）\n- **aoao（熬熬）**：诊断与交付工程师（Diagnostics & Delivery）\n\n---\n\n## 本轮重点模块\n只打一轮，不贪多。\n\n### 首轮重点\n1. `gateway`\n2. `sessions / subagents`\n3. `Feishu / message tool`\n4. `docs walkthrough`\n\n### 为什么是这 4 个\n- 都是主流程\n- 最容易影响新用户和真实使用\n- 最容易出现“文档写了，但实际不通”这种高价值问题\n- 当前多 agent / Feishu 环境已具备，适合直接测\n\n---\n\n## 第 1 周拆解\n\n### Day 1：今天要完成的事\n1. 定 bug 分类\n2. 定 issue 提交标准\n3. 建 bug 候选池\n4. 明确首轮重点模块\n5. 建项目目录与文档骨架\n\n### Day 2-3\n1. xixi 拉线索 + 复现候选问题\n2. main 直接抓取 xixi / aoao 的 session history 做每日 triage\n3. aoao 对高价值候选做诊断分流\n\n### Day 4-5\n1. 聚焦前 5-10 条候选问题\n2. 过滤误报 / 重复 / feature request\n3. 输出首批 issue / PR / docs fix 3-5 条\n\n---\n\n## Bug 分类\n- `logic`：逻辑错误 / 行为错误\n- `regression`：版本回归\n- `docs`：文档与实际不一致\n- `config`：配置缺失 / 配置错误引发的问题\n- `compatibility`：系统 / Node / 环境兼容性\n- `ux`：提示差、错误信息误导、流程不顺\n- `integration`：多组件联动问题（如 gateway + Feishu + sessions）\n\n---\n\n## Issue 提交标准\n只有同时满足下面条件，才允许进入正式提交：\n\n1. **有最小复现步骤**\n2. **有环境信息**\n3. **有预期/实际对比**\n4. **有日志或可验证现象**\n5. **已做重复检查**\n6. **能明确归入 issue / PR / docs fix / 内部留档 之一**\n\n不满足就不提，宁缺毋滥。\n\n---\n\n## 验收标准\n本轮阶段验收不是“测了很多”，而是：\n\n1. 项目资料全部归档到统一目录\n2. 候选池建立完成\n3. 至少形成 5 条标准化候选问题卡\n4. 至少筛出 3 条值得继续追的高价值问题\n5. 每条问题都有明确去向：issue / PR / docs fix / 内部留档\n\n---\n\n## 风险点\n1. **范围失控**：一上来全模块开测，结果全浅尝辄止\n2. **低质量 issue**：没有证据就下判断\n3. **角色混乱**：复现、诊断、交付职责搅在一起\n4. **只发现不闭环**：有候选池，没有交付物\n5. **文档漂移**：计划在群里、资料在本地、结论没统一落档\n6. **回执假阻塞**：agent 实际已完成，但 `sessions_send` timeout 导致 main 误判为“未回执”\n\n---\n\n## 当前动作清单\n- [x] 创建项目目录\n- [x] 归档原始项目计划\n- [x] 明确 3 人角色映射\n- [x] 明确首轮重点模块\n- [x] 输出执行方案 v1\n- [x] 建 bug 候选池表\n- [x] 建 bug 记录卡模板\n- [x] 向 xixi 下发线索/复现任务\n- [x] 向 aoao 下发诊断/交付任务\n- [x] 已拿到 xixi / aoao 的 session 结果\n- [ ] 将 session 结果并入候选池与 triage\n- [ ] 开始首轮 triage\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1774236723721}}
{"type":"message","id":"c92b6ea2","parentId":"a3849331","timestamp":"2026-03-23T03:32:03.752Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_CHaadHGQfwZkRpkh1rTUzGmF|fc_0c5151d58c45418b0169c0b43367a481918504e9da629b89a6","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Contributing to OpenClaw\n\nWelcome to the lobster tank! 🦞\n\n## Quick Links\n\n- **GitHub:** https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw\n- **Vision:** [`VISION.md`](VISION.md)\n- **Discord:** https://discord.gg/qkhbAGHRBT\n- **X/Twitter:** [@steipete](https://x.com/steipete) / [@openclaw](https://x.com/openclaw)\n\n## Maintainers\n\n- **Peter Steinberger** - Benevolent Dictator\n  - GitHub: [@steipete](https://github.com/steipete) · X: [@steipete](https://x.com/steipete)\n\n- **Shadow** - Discord subsystem, Discord admin, Clawhub, all community moderation\n  - GitHub: [@thewilloftheshadow](https://github.com/thewilloftheshadow) · X: [@4shadowed](https://x.com/4shadowed)\n\n- **Vignesh** - Memory (QMD), formal modeling, TUI, IRC, and Lobster\n  - GitHub: [@vignesh07](https://github.com/vignesh07) · X: [@\\_vgnsh](https://x.com/_vgnsh)\n\n- **Jos** - Telegram, API, Nix mode\n  - GitHub: [@joshp123](https://github.com/joshp123) · X: [@jjpcodes](https://x.com/jjpcodes)\n\n- **Ayaan Zaidi** - Telegram subsystem, Android app\n  - GitHub: [@obviyus](https://github.com/obviyus) · X: [@0bviyus](https://x.com/0bviyus)\n\n- **Tyler Yust** - Agents/subagents, cron, BlueBubbles, macOS app\n  - GitHub: [@tyler6204](https://github.com/tyler6204) · X: [@tyleryust](https://x.com/tyleryust)\n\n- **Mariano Belinky** - iOS app, Security\n  - GitHub: [@mbelinky](https://github.com/mbelinky) · X: [@belimad](https://x.com/belimad)\n\n- **Nimrod Gutman** - iOS app, macOS app and crustacean features\n  - GitHub: [@ngutman](https://github.com/ngutman) · X: [@theguti](https://x.com/theguti)\n\n- **Vincent Koc** - Agents, Telemetry, Hooks, Security\n  - GitHub: [@vincentkoc](https://github.com/vincentkoc) · X: [@vincent_koc](https://x.com/vincent_koc)\n\n- **Val Alexander** - UI/UX, Docs, and Agent DevX\n  - GitHub: [@BunsDev](https://github.com/BunsDev) · X: [@BunsDev](https://x.com/BunsDev)\n\n- **Seb Slight** - Docs, Agent Reliability, Runtime Hardening\n  - GitHub: [@sebslight](https://github.com/sebslight) · X: [@sebslig](https://x.com/sebslig)\n\n- **Christoph Nakazawa** - JS Infra\n  - GitHub: [@cpojer](https://github.com/cpojer) · X: [@cnakazawa](https://x.com/cnakazawa)\n\n- **Gustavo Madeira Santana** - Multi-agents, CLI, Performance, Plugins, Matrix\n  - GitHub: [@gumadeiras](https://github.com/gumadeiras) · X: [@gumadeiras](https://x.com/gumadeiras)\n\n- **Onur Solmaz** - Agents, dev workflows, ACP integrations, MS Teams\n  - GitHub: [@onutc](https://github.com/onutc), [@osolmaz](https://github.com/osolmaz) · X: [@onusoz](https://x.com/onusoz)\n\n- **Josh Avant** - Core, CLI, Gateway, Security, Agents\n  - GitHub: [@joshavant](https://github.com/joshavant) · X: [@joshavant](https://x.com/joshavant)\n\n- **Jonathan Taylor** - ACP subsystem, Gateway features/bugs, Gog/Mog/Sog CLI's, SEDMAT\n  - GitHub [@visionik](https://github.com/visionik) · X: [@visionik](https://x.com/visionik)\n- **Josh Lehman** - Compaction, Tlon/Urbit subsystem\n  - GitHub [@jalehman](https://github.com/jalehman) · X: [@jlehman\\_](https://x.com/jlehman_)\n\n- **Radek Sienkiewicz** - Docs, Control UI\n  - GitHub [@velvet-shark](https://github.com/velvet-shark) · X: [@velvet_shark](https://twitter.com/velvet_shark)\n\n- **Muhammed Mukhthar** - Mattermost, CLI\n  - GitHub [@mukhtharcm](https://github.com/mukhtharcm) · X: [@mukhtharcm](https://x.com/mukhtharcm)\n\n- **Altay** - Agents, CLI, error handling\n  - GitHub [@altaywtf](https://github.com/altaywtf) · X: [@altaywtf](https://x.com/altaywtf)\n\n- **Robin Waslander** - Security, PR triage, bug fixes\n  - GitHub: [@hydro13](https://github.com/hydro13) · X: [@Robin_waslander](https://x.com/Robin_waslander)\n\n- **Tengji (George) Zhang** - Chinese model APIs, cloud, pi\n  - GitHub: [@odysseus0](https://github.com/odysseus0) · X: [@odysseus0z](https://x.com/odysseus0z)\n\n- **Andrew (Bubbles) Demczuk** - Agents/Gateway/TTS/VTT\n  - GitHub: [@ademczuk](https://github.com/ademczuk) · X: [@ademczuk](https://x.com/ademczuk)\n\n## How to Contribute\n\n1. **Bugs & small fixes** → Open a PR!\n2. **New features / architecture** → Start a [GitHub Discussion](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/discussions) or ask in Discord first\n3. **Refactor-only PRs** → Don't open a PR. We are not accepting refactor-only changes unless a maintainer explicitly asks for them as part of a concrete fix.\n4. **Test/CI-only PRs for known `main` failures** → Don't open a PR. The Maintainer team is already tracking those failures, and PRs that only tweak tests or CI to chase them will be closed unless they are required to validate a new fix.\n5. **Questions** → Discord [#help](https://discord.com/channels/1456350064065904867/1459642797895319552) / [#users-helping-users](https://discord.com/channels/1456350064065904867/1459007081603403828)\n\n## Before You PR\n\n- Test locally with your OpenClaw instance\n- Run tests: `pnpm build && pnpm check && pnpm test`\n- For extension/plugin changes, run the fast local lane first:\n  - `pnpm test:extension <extension-name>`\n  - `pnpm test:extension --list` to see valid extension ids\n  - If you changed shared plugin or channel surfaces, run `pnpm test:contracts`\n  - For targeted shared-surface work, use `pnpm test:contracts:channels` or `pnpm test:contracts:plugins`\n  - If you changed broader runtime behavior, still run the relevant wider lanes (`pnpm test:extensions`, `pnpm test:channels`, or `pnpm test`) before asking for review\n- If you have access to Codex, run `codex review --base origin/main` locally before opening or updating your PR. Treat this as the current highest standard of AI review, even if GitHub Codex review also runs.\n- Do not submit refactor-only PRs unless a maintainer explicitly requested that refactor for an active fix or deliverable.\n- Do not submit test or CI-config fixes for failures already red on `main` CI. If a failure is already visible in the [main branch CI runs](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions), it's a known issue the Maintainer team is tracking, and a PR that only addresses those failures will be closed automatically. If you spot a _new_ regression not yet shown in main CI, report it as an issue first.\n- Do not submit test-only PRs that just try to make known `main` CI failures pass. Test changes are acceptable when they are required to validate a new fix or cover new behavior in the same PR.\n- Ensure CI checks pass\n- Keep PRs focused (one thing per PR; do not mix unrelated concerns)\n- Describe what & why\n- Reply to or resolve bot review conversations you addressed before asking for review again\n- **Include screenshots** — one showing the problem/before, one showing the fix/after (for UI or visual changes)\n- Use American English spelling and grammar in code, comments, docs, and UI strings\n- Do not edit files covered by `CODEOWNERS` security ownership unless a listed owner explicitly asked for the change or is already reviewing it with you. Treat those paths as restricted review surfaces, not opportunistic cleanup targets.\n\n## Review Conversations Are Author-Owned\n\nIf a review bot leaves review conversations on your PR, you are expected to handle the follow-through:\n\n- Resolve the conversation yourself once the code or explanation fully addresses the bot's concern\n- Reply and leave it open only when you need maintainer or reviewer judgment\n- Do not leave \"fixed\" bot review conversations for maintainers to clean up for you\n- If Codex leaves comments, address every relevant one or resolve it with a short explanation when it is not applicable to your change\n- If GitHub Codex review does not trigger for some reason, run `codex review --base origin/main` locally anyway and treat that output as required review work\n\nThis applies to both human-authored and AI-assisted PRs.\n\n## Control UI Decorators\n\nThe Control UI uses Lit with **legacy** decorators (current Rollup parsing does not support\n`accessor` fields required for standard decorators). When adding reactive fields, keep the\nlegacy style:\n\n```ts\n@state() foo = \"bar\";\n@property({ type: Number }) count = 0;\n```\n\nThe root `tsconfig.json` is configured for legacy decorators (`experimentalDecorators: true`)\nwith `useDefineForClassFields: false`. Avoid flipping these unless you are also updating the UI\nbuild tooling to support standard decorators.\n\n## AI/Vibe-Coded PRs Welcome! 🤖\n\nBuilt with Codex, Claude, or other AI tools? **Awesome - just mark it!**\n\nPlease include in your PR:\n\n- [ ] Mark as AI-assisted in the PR title or description\n- [ ] Note the degree of testing (untested / lightly tested / fully tested)\n- [ ] Include prompts or session logs if possible (super helpful!)\n- [ ] Confirm you understand what the code does\n- [ ] If you have access to Codex, run `codex review --base origin/main` locally and address the findings before asking for review\n- [ ] Resolve or reply to bot review conversations after you address them\n\nAI PRs are first-class citizens here. We just want transparency so reviewers know what to look for. If you are using an LLM coding agent, instruct it to resolve bot review conversations it has addressed instead of leaving them for maintainers.\n\n## Current Focus & Roadmap 🗺\n\nWe are currently prioritizing:\n\n- **Stability**: Fixing edge cases in channel connections (WhatsApp/Telegram).\n- **UX**: Improving the onboarding wizard and error messages.\n- **Skills**: For skill contributions, head to [ClawHub](https://clawhub.ai/) — the community hub for OpenClaw skills.\n- **Performance**: Optimizing token usage and compaction logic.\n\nCheck the [GitHub Issues](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues) for \"good first issue\" labels!\n\n## Maintainers\n\nWe're selectively expanding the maintainer team.\nIf you're an experienced contributor who wants to help shape OpenClaw's direction — whether through code, docs, or community — we'd like to hear from you.\n\nBeing a maintainer is a responsibility, not an honorary title. We expect active, consistent involvement — triaging issues, reviewing PRs, and helping move the project forward.\n\nStill interested? Email contributing@openclaw.ai with:\n\n- Links to your PRs on OpenClaw (if you don't have any, start there first)\n- Links to open source projects you maintain or actively contribute to\n- Your GitHub, Discord, and X/Twitter handles\n- A brief intro: background, experience, and areas of interest\n- Languages you speak and where you're based\n- How much time you can realistically commit\n\nWe welcome people across all skill sets — engineering, documentation, community management, and more.\nWe review every human-only-written application carefully and add maintainers slowly and deliberately.\nPlease allow a few weeks for a response.\n\n## Report a Vulnerability\n\nWe take security reports seriously. Report vulnerabilities directly to the repository where the issue lives:\n\n- **Core CLI and gateway** — [openclaw/openclaw](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw)\n- **macOS desktop app** — [openclaw/openclaw](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw) (apps/macos)\n- **iOS app** — [openclaw/openclaw](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw) (apps/ios)\n- **Android app** — [openclaw/openclaw](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw) (apps/android)\n- **ClawHub** — [openclaw/clawhub](https://github.com/openclaw/clawhub)\n- **Trust and threat model** — [openclaw/trust](https://github.com/openclaw/trust)\n\nFor issues that don't fit a specific repo, or if you're unsure, email **security@openclaw.ai** and we'll route it.\n\n### Required in Reports\n\n1. **Title**\n2. **Severity Assessment**\n3. **Impact**\n4. **Affected Component**\n5. **Technical Reproduction**\n6. **Demonstrated Impact**\n7. **Environment**\n8. **Remediation Advice**\n\nReports without reproduction steps, demonstrated impact, and remediation advice will be deprioritized. Given the volume of AI-generated scanner findings, we must ensure we're receiving vetted reports from researchers who understand the issues.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1774236723743}}
{"type":"message","id":"377cef3d","parentId":"c92b6ea2","timestamp":"2026-03-23T03:32:03.772Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_lHtR5dZKK6fmLXb4vhMBN8ar|fc_0c5151d58c45418b0169c0b43367a88191b30cebf2c237310f","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\ntitle: CI Pipeline\nsummary: \"CI job graph, scope gates, and local command equivalents\"\nread_when:\n  - You need to understand why a CI job did or did not run\n  - You are debugging failing GitHub Actions checks\n---\n\n# CI Pipeline\n\nThe CI runs on every push to `main` and every pull request. It uses smart scoping to skip expensive jobs when only unrelated areas changed.\n\n## Job Overview\n\n| Job               | Purpose                                                 | When it runs                       |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `docs-scope`      | Detect docs-only changes                                | Always                             |\n| `changed-scope`   | Detect which areas changed (node/macos/android/windows) | Non-doc changes                    |\n| `check`           | TypeScript types, lint, format                          | Non-docs, node changes             |\n| `check-docs`      | Markdown lint + broken link check                       | Docs changed                       |\n| `secrets`         | Detect leaked secrets                                   | Always                             |\n| `build-artifacts` | Build dist once, share with `release-check`             | Pushes to `main`, node changes     |\n| `release-check`   | Validate npm pack contents                              | Pushes to `main` after build       |\n| `checks`          | Node tests + protocol check on PRs; Bun compat on push  | Non-docs, node changes             |\n| `compat-node22`   | Minimum supported Node runtime compatibility            | Pushes to `main`, node changes     |\n| `checks-windows`  | Windows-specific tests                                  | Non-docs, windows-relevant changes |\n| `macos`           | Swift lint/build/test + TS tests                        | PRs with macos changes             |\n| `android`         | Gradle build + tests                                    | Non-docs, android changes          |\n\n## Fail-Fast Order\n\nJobs are ordered so cheap checks fail before expensive ones run:\n\n1. `docs-scope` + `changed-scope` + `check` + `secrets` (parallel, cheap gates first)\n2. PRs: `checks` (Linux Node test split into 2 shards), `checks-windows`, `macos`, `android`\n3. Pushes to `main`: `build-artifacts` + `release-check` + Bun compat + `compat-node22`\n\nScope logic lives in `scripts/ci-changed-scope.mjs` and is covered by unit tests in `src/scripts/ci-changed-scope.test.ts`.\nThe same shared scope module also drives the separate `install-smoke` workflow through a narrower `changed-smoke` gate, so Docker/install smoke only runs for install, packaging, and container-relevant changes.\n\n## Runners\n\n| Runner                           | Jobs                                       |\n| -------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `blacksmith-16vcpu-ubuntu-2404`  | Most Linux jobs, including scope detection |\n| `blacksmith-32vcpu-windows-2025` | `checks-windows`                           |\n| `macos-latest`                   | `macos`, `ios`                             |\n\n## Local Equivalents\n\n```bash\npnpm check          # types + lint + format\npnpm test           # vitest tests\npnpm check:docs     # docs format + lint + broken links\npnpm release:check  # validate npm pack\n```\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1774236723763}}
{"type":"message","id":"83112936","parentId":"377cef3d","timestamp":"2026-03-23T03:32:03.794Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_TwV5FvLl0gOSZgRrQ2LKzvrT|fc_0c5151d58c45418b0169c0b43367ac8191975c1a44f13786a1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Summary\n\nDescribe the problem and fix in 2–5 bullets:\n\n- Problem:\n- Why it matters:\n- What changed:\n- What did NOT change (scope boundary):\n\n## Change Type (select all)\n\n- [ ] Bug fix\n- [ ] Feature\n- [ ] Refactor required for the fix\n- [ ] Docs\n- [ ] Security hardening\n- [ ] Chore/infra\n\n## Scope (select all touched areas)\n\n- [ ] Gateway / orchestration\n- [ ] Skills / tool execution\n- [ ] Auth / tokens\n- [ ] Memory / storage\n- [ ] Integrations\n- [ ] API / contracts\n- [ ] UI / DX\n- [ ] CI/CD / infra\n\n## Linked Issue/PR\n\n- Closes #\n- Related #\n\n## User-visible / Behavior Changes\n\nList user-visible changes (including defaults/config).  \nIf none, write `None`.\n\n## Security Impact (required)\n\n- New permissions/capabilities? (`Yes/No`)\n- Secrets/tokens handling changed? (`Yes/No`)\n- New/changed network calls? (`Yes/No`)\n- Command/tool execution surface changed? (`Yes/No`)\n- Data access scope changed? (`Yes/No`)\n- If any `Yes`, explain risk + mitigation:\n\n## Repro + Verification\n\n### Environment\n\n- OS:\n- Runtime/container:\n- Model/provider:\n- Integration/channel (if any):\n- Relevant config (redacted):\n\n### Steps\n\n1.\n2.\n3.\n\n### Expected\n\n-\n\n### Actual\n\n-\n\n## Evidence\n\nAttach at least one:\n\n- [ ] Failing test/log before + passing after\n- [ ] Trace/log snippets\n- [ ] Screenshot/recording\n- [ ] Perf numbers (if relevant)\n\n## Human Verification (required)\n\nWhat you personally verified (not just CI), and how:\n\n- Verified scenarios:\n- Edge cases checked:\n- What you did **not** verify:\n\n## Review Conversations\n\n- [ ] I replied to or resolved every bot review conversation I addressed in this PR.\n- [ ] I left unresolved only the conversations that still need reviewer or maintainer judgment.\n\nIf a bot review conversation is addressed by this PR, resolve that conversation yourself. Do not leave bot review conversation cleanup for maintainers.\n\n## Compatibility / Migration\n\n- Backward compatible? (`Yes/No`)\n- Config/env changes? (`Yes/No`)\n- Migration needed? (`Yes/No`)\n- If yes, exact upgrade steps:\n\n## Failure Recovery (if this breaks)\n\n- How to disable/revert this change quickly:\n- Files/config to restore:\n- Known bad symptoms reviewers should watch for:\n\n## Risks and Mitigations\n\nList only real risks for this PR. Add/remove entries as needed. If none, write `None`.\n\n- Risk:\n  - Mitigation:\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1774236723782}}
{"type":"message","id":"c53827ae","parentId":"83112936","timestamp":"2026-03-23T03:32:11.862Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_P5ZXFPw9wd778x7NYjIQHRmv|fc_0c5151d58c45418b0169c0b43b9ff8819180d8d80a58037e2e","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"git -C /root/.openclaw/workspace/projects/openclaw-pr remote -v && printf '\\n---branch---\\n' && git -C /root/.openclaw/workspace/projects/openclaw-pr branch --show-current && printf '\\n---status---\\n' && git -C /root/.openclaw/workspace/projects/openclaw-pr status --short && printf '\\n---pr status---\\n' && gh pr status --repo openclaw/openclaw && printf '\\n---my open prs---\\n' && gh pr list --repo openclaw/openclaw --author EronFan --state open --limit 20 && printf '\\n---my open prs json---\\n' && gh pr list --repo openclaw/openclaw --author EronFan --state open --json number,title,url,reviewDecision,headRefName,isDraft,statusCheckRollup,updatedAt","workdir":"/root/.openclaw/workspace","yieldMs":10000,"timeout":90},"partialJson":"{\"command\":\"git -C /root/.openclaw/workspace/projects/openclaw-pr remote -v && printf '\\\\n---branch---\\\\n' && git -C /root/.openclaw/workspace/projects/openclaw-pr branch --show-current && printf '\\\\n---status---\\\\n' && git -C /root/.openclaw/workspace/projects/openclaw-pr status --short && printf '\\\\n---pr status---\\\\n' && gh pr status --repo openclaw/openclaw && printf '\\\\n---my open prs---\\\\n' && gh pr list --repo openclaw/openclaw --author EronFan --state open --limit 20 && printf '\\\\n---my open prs json---\\\\n' && gh pr list --repo openclaw/openclaw --author EronFan --state open --json number,title,url,reviewDecision,headRefName,isDraft,statusCheckRollup,updatedAt\",\"workdir\":\"/root/.openclaw/workspace\",\"yieldMs\":10000,\"timeout\":90}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_qyqKOAxUKaOmCZ6tJC74WInW|fc_0c5151d58c45418b0169c0b43ba00881919d5859d2110eead2","name":"sessions_history","arguments":{"sessionKey":"agent:xixi:feishu:xixi:d