/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/23419803591/job/68122381711\",\"name\":\"checks-windows (node, test, 5, 6, pnpm test)\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-03-23T03:14:02Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"CI\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-03-23T03:15:27Z\",\"conclusion\":\"FAILURE\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/23419803591/job/68122381707\",\"name\":\"checks-windows (node, test, 6, 6, pnpm test)\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-03-23T03:13:28Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"CI\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-03-23T03:14:00Z\",\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://greptile.com/\",\"name\":\"Greptile Review\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-03-23T03:12:08Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"\"}],\"updatedAt\":\"2026-03-23T03:14:59Z\"}"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":716,"aggregated":"{\"comments\":[{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOQb6kR8701sGO\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"greptile-apps\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"CONTRIBUTOR\",\"body\":\"<h3>Greptile Summary</h3>\\n\\nThis PR fixes a double skill registration bug in the Feishu extension by removing the static `\\\"skills\\\": [\\\"./skills\\\"]` entry from `extensions/feishu/openclaw.plugin.json` (and the corresponding generated metadata file). All Feishu tools are already registered programmatically through `registerFull()` in `index.ts`, making the static `skills` path redundant.\\n\\n- Removes `\\\"skills\\\": [\\\"./skills\\\"]` from the Feishu plugin manifest — the `skills/` directory contains only `SKILL.md` documentation files, not code, and `registerFull()` is the single source of truth for tool registration.\\n- Updates `bundled-plugin-metadata.generated.ts` to stay in sync with the manifest change.\\n- `registerFull()` and all channel/runtime setup in `index.ts` are untouched, so functionality is fully preserved.\\n- 472 tests passed after the change per the author.\\n\\n<h3>Confidence Score: 5/5</h3>\\n\\n- Safe to merge — the change is a minimal, targeted removal of a duplicate registration entry with no functional side effects.\\n- The fix is a two-line removal that addresses a clearly identified root cause. `registerFull()` remains the sole authoritative registration path, the `skills/` directory only held documentation (`SKILL.md`) files rather than code, and the generated file is correctly kept in sync. The full test suite (472 tests) passed after the change.\\n- No files require special attention.\\n\\n<!-- greptile_other_comments_section -->\\n\\n<sub>Reviews (1): Last reviewed commit: [\\\"fix(feishu): avoid double skill registra...\\\"](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/commit/c002c6c21a5f1d036e3dcfd986b3254f1a44f363) | [Re-trigger Greptile](https://app.greptile.com/api/retrigger?id=25999570)</sub>\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-03-23T03:13:59Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/52597#issuecomment-4107714958\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":false}],\"reviews\":[{\"id\":\"PRR_kwDOQb6kR87txNWJ\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"NONE\",\"body\":\"\\n### 💡 Codex Review\\n\\nHere are some automated review suggestions for this pull request.\\n\\n**Reviewed commit:** `c002c6c21a`\\n    \\n\\n<details> <summary>ℹ️ About Codex in GitHub</summary>\\n<br/>\\n\\nCodex has been enabled to automatically review pull requests in this repo. Reviews are triggered when you\\n- Open a pull request for review\\n- Mark a draft as ready\\n- Comment \\\"@codex review\\\".\\n\\nIf Codex has suggestions, it will comment; otherwise it will react with 👍.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nWhen you [sign up for Codex through ChatGPT](https://openai.com/codex), Codex can also answer questions or update the PR, like \\\"@codex address that feedback\\\".\\n            \\n</details>\",\"submittedAt\":\"2026-03-23T03:14:59Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"react